SOC Incident Report – Phishing Email Investigation

Incident ID: SOC-2026-03-05
Alert Type: Suspicious Email with External Link
Date: 2026-03-05
Analyst: Yusuke Fujita
Severity: Medium
Status: Confirmed Phishing – User Interaction Observed

1. Executive Summary

On March 5, 2026, the SOC received an alert for an inbound email containing an external link with suspicious characteristics. The message impersonated Microsoft security and attempted to lure the recipient into reviewing a fake sign-in alert.
Analysis identified a typosquatted domain (m1crosoftsupport.co) used to mimic legitimate Microsoft infrastructure.
Correlation with firewall logs confirmed that the recipient endpoint attempted and successfully established an outbound connection to the phishing domain. This indicates the user likely clicked the link in the email.
The incident was classified as confirmed phishing with user interaction, requiring endpoint verification and account security checks.

