8. Impact Assessment

Potential risks include:
Credential harvesting
Account compromise
Unauthorized access to Microsoft services
Business Email Compromise (BEC)
Because the connection was allowed, credential entry cannot be ruled out without further investigation.

9. Containment & Remediation
Immediate response actions recommended:
Account Security
Force password reset for user
Revoke active authentication sessions
Verify MFA status
Endpoint Investigation
Scan endpoint for malware
Review browser history and downloads
Analyze endpoint telemetry
Network Security
Block domain m1crosoftsupport.co
Block IP 45.148.10.131
Add domain to email filtering rules
User Awareness
Notify user of phishing attempt
Provide phishing awareness guidance

10. Lessons Learned

Typosquatting domains remain a common phishing tactic.
URL-based phishing can bypass initial email filtering.
Rapid correlation between email alerts and firewall logs is critical for identifying user interaction.

Improvement opportunities:
Enable automated URL detonation or sandboxing
Strengthen phishing awareness training
Expand domain reputation monitoring
